From b8593217966dd870fe8d1477b82d9bb842117f00 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: local <local@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 00:15:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 26/34] WP17: Copy cleanup on guest and host pages

Conflict resolution: the app.css?v= key in the three base templates goes to 20261004z (after WP01's a, WP28's w and WP08's y; guest.css has its own 20261004z). guest/stay.html: WP17 removed the Ticket Wallet keep-this-page line, which main's arrival-lane stay page no longer has; main's version kept. Guest languages (WP26 is earlier in this order): for every guest key WP17 changed in EN and CS, the de/es/fr texts now say the same thing (legal_intro, host_details_help, claim_help, claim_email_help, assigned_body, pin_help, someone_missing, residence_help, passport_photo_help, legal_notice_duty_body, legal_notice_reporting_body, privacy), and the 15 keys WP17 deleted are deleted in de/es/fr too. Main's arrival-lane claim form shows only claim_email_help, so it gains the tw_email_short hint ("We send your private link here. No marketing.") that WP17's shorter help text relies on. WP27's house book storage row: WP17 removes the house book intro dialog that wrote ubyhost_housebook_legal_v1, so the row (and its de/es/fr text) is gone from cookie_inventory.py and tests/test_cookie_inventory.py only asserts that the storage scan found keys. Test updates: tests/test_guest_languages.py checks the six years in privacy instead of the deleted why_point_book; tests/test_guest_confirm_screen.py finds the confirm card by its heading (main has no tw_label_confirm).
